   "body": "**Adversarial review (Opus 5.5, cloud/review-1229-opus, round 1): REQUEST CHANGES** — head f0356214\n\n1. **High**, `App/SwiftHFRTests/Favorites/TopicRowActionsTests.swift:255`: the new test fails.\n   - **Why it fails:** `favoritesList(...)` defaults to `source: .flagged` (helper at :10-11). `menuOffersFilter` requires `source == .favorites` (`TopicListModel+RowActions.swift:47`). So `#expect(model.menuOffersFilter(flaggedTopic(2), filterIsBusy: false))` is false, the test goes red, and `compile-check` / the app test job fails.\n   - **The busy check proves nothing:** the next line (`filterIsBusy: true` → false) passes for the wrong reason, because the source check alone makes it false.\n   - **A claim with no assertion:** the doc comment says « absent off Favoris », but nothing checks it.\n   - **Fix:** build a second model with `favoritesList([...], source: .favorites)`. On it, assert true when not busy and false when busy. On the `.flagged` model, assert false (absent off Favoris). Run it on the Mac or in CI before asking for round 2.\n\n2. **Low**, `App/SwiftHFR/Navigation/TopicListView.swift:246-247`: the test checks only the two model predicates, not the menu wiring.\n   - **Scenario:** if the view goes back to `removeButton` / `.disabled(filtering.isBusy)` with the old conditions, every test stays green (LESSONS L01).\n   - **Fix:** say in the PR body that the menu itself is checked by hand on the next device review (#893), or add a hosted check if a cheap one exists.\n\n3. **Detail**, `TopicListView.swift:234`: the `Divider()` after « Copier le lien » is always built.\n   - **When it shows up:** on a Drapeaux row while its removal is in flight, nothing may follow it (no « Lu » on `.unknown` read state, possibly no super favourite).\n   - **Impact:** SwiftUI should drop a trailing divider in a menu. No change asked; look at it on the device review.\n\n**Checked, no finding:**\n- `menu(...)` is only used by `.contextMenu` (:197). The trailing swipe (:188) still uses `canRemoveFlag` with `removeButton`'s `.disabled(removing)`, and the VoiceOver `accessibilityActions` (:190-195) are unchanged.\n- `menuOffersFilter` keeps the previous conditions (`.favorites`, `filtering` non-nil, `topicID`). If a filter run starts while the menu is open, `FilteredPostsModel.start` already refuses to run (`guard !isRunning, !isAdvancing`).\n- #1163: all five places are first loads; the error and retry branches come before them. No `accessibilityLabel` or identifier hangs on those views, no UI test uses the captions, and « Recherche des … » (MessageListView:94) and FilteredPostsView:61/:204 are left alone. What the PR body says it leaves out (Catégories, reader, GIF picker) and why #1163 has no test is accurate.\n\n**Vérifié**\n- `git diff origin/dev-swift...f0356214`.\n- Read issues #1162 and #1163 and the PR body.\n- Read `TopicSource` and the test helpers: `.flagged` ≠ `.favorites`, so finding 1 comes from reading the code. App tests cannot run on Linux.\n- grep for `ProgressView` / `Chargement` in the app and the UI tests.\n- SwiftLint on the touched files in a throwaway worktree: clean. The worktree is removed.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
