   "body": "**Adversarial review (Opus 5.5, cloud/review-1229-opus-r2, round 2): APPROVE** — head 7e89d7d6\n\nRound 1 finding 1 is fixed. Only `App/SwiftHFRTests/Favorites/TopicRowActionsTests.swift` changed since f0356214 (+9/−2).\n\n1. **Detail**, `TopicRowActionsTests.swift:237-238` and the PR body. The doc comment and the Tests section both say \"Supprimer\" \"shows again after\", but no test checks that. It also cannot happen: the removal is confirmed, so the row leaves the list. Fix: drop \"and shows it again after\" from both. Another way: script an unconfirmed or refused removal and then assert `menuOffersRemove(topic)`.\n\nRound 1 finding 2 (the menu wiring has no test) is accepted. The PR body says the #893 device review checks it by hand. Finding 3 (the trailing Divider) is unchanged and not blocking.\n\n**Vérifié**\n- `git diff f0356214..7e89d7d6 --stat`: one test file changed, no production change since round 1.\n- I read the whole PR again (7 files).\n- `favoritesList` already had a `source:` parameter (default `.flagged`). It builds `TopicListModel(source:dataSource:isLoggedIn:flagActions:)` without `favorites:`. That init exists and defaults the options to nil. Several tests already build `.favorites` models this way, so this compiles. The Compile check is green on 7e89d7d6.\n- `menuOffersFilter` reads only `source`, `topic.topicID` and the busy flag, so it does not depend on the load. `flaggedTopic(2)` has a `TopicID`, so it returns true on Favoris when idle.\n- Each test fails without its part of the change:\n  - without `!filterIsBusy`, the new test fails;\n  - without the `source == .favorites` check, the last expect of the Drapeaux test fails;\n  - without `!isRemovingFlag`, the in-flight expect fails;\n  - without the new methods, nothing compiles.\n- #1163 covers exactly the five sites the issue lists. The captions left out on purpose (forums, reader, GIF picker, searches) are named in the PR body.\n- SwiftLint on the changed paths in a throwaway worktree: rc=0. The worktree is removed.\n- App tests not run (Linux).\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
